# 4. Spread and Rest Operators

The `...` syntax is used for both:

```text
Spread Operator
Rest Operator
```

Although they use the same syntax, their purposes are different.

---

# 🔹 Spread Operator

The **spread operator** expands elements of an array or properties of an object.

---

## Array Spread

```javascript
const numbers1 = [1, 2, 3];

const numbers2 = [...numbers1, 4, 5];

console.log(numbers2);
```

Output:

```text
[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
```

---

## Combining Arrays

```javascript
const fruits = ["Apple", "Mango"];
const vegetables = ["Carrot", "Potato"];

const food = [...fruits, ...vegetables];

console.log(food);
```

Output:

```text
["Apple", "Mango", "Carrot", "Potato"]
```

---

## Object Spread

```javascript
const user = {
    name: "Abhinav",
    age: 20
};

const updatedUser = {
    ...user,
    skill: "React"
};

console.log(updatedUser);
```

Output:

```text
{
    name: "Abhinav",
    age: 20,
    skill: "React"
}
```

---

## 🔥 Spread in React State

Spread is commonly used when updating objects or arrays without directly modifying the original value.

```javascript
const user = {
    name: "Abhinav",
    age: 20
};

const updatedUser = {
    ...user,
    age: 21
};

console.log(updatedUser);
```

This creates a new object with the updated property.

---

# 🔹 Rest Operator

The **rest operator** collects multiple values into a single array.

```javascript
function add(...numbers) {
    console.log(numbers);
}

add(10, 20, 30, 40);
```

Output:

```text
[10, 20, 30, 40]
```

---

## 🔹 Rest with Parameters

```javascript
function sum(...numbers) {
    return numbers.reduce((total, number) => total + number, 0);
}

console.log(sum(10, 20, 30));
```

Output:

```text
60
```

---

## 🔹 Rest with Destructuring

```javascript
const numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40];

const [first, ...remaining] = numbers;

console.log(first);
console.log(remaining);
```

Output:

```text
10
[20, 30, 40]
```

---

## ⭐ Spread vs Rest

| Spread `...` | Rest `...` |
|---|---|
| Expands values | Collects values |
| Used to copy/combine | Used to group remaining values |
| Arrays and objects | Function parameters/destructuring |
| `const copy = [...array]` | `function test(...args)` |

### Easy way to remember:

```text
SPREAD → Expand 📤

REST → Collect 📥
```

